    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d943">

                <pb facs="0841" n="725" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg725"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/15422.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Brazilian Minister to Mexico</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-14T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 14, 1915—4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>813. Your No. 671, July 11, 1 p.m. As crisis in Mexico City has passed,
                    Department will send its 808, July 8, 6 p.m., to Carothers instead of having you
                    deliver it to Conventionists.</p>
                <p>Department gratified at splendid work done by you, in conjunction with
                    colleagues, in recent Mexico City crisis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
